difference:
The first reader's list is right but incomplete. BW1 also:
- sets the flashlight max_distance to 32.0 (nocedit 64.0) and resets special_view_active;
- clears field notes and releases puzzle graphics at session start, and loads and frees the cursor bitmaps;
- switches to 640x480 while a puzzle or the field notes are up;
- on a non-alive hero clears goggles and closes the field notes and puzzle (activatePuzzle(p,0));
- when selected_camera_index < 0, sets focus_actor_changed=2 and forces the director;
- ignores Escape while CDemonMission::teleport_requested is set;
- has Escape close the field notes, then the puzzle, before the pause menu;
- calls resetIrisFade before skipCinematic;
- handles the dialog even when item_count < 1;
- clears the screen for the first 3 presented frames (screen_clear_count);
- raises the persistent event 'NewSet' while new_set_event_pending (set by CDemonMission::loadSet);
- reads a dev Ctrl+P;
- drops the memory checks.

BW2:
- prints a ' ' line and CGameHook::printBanner;
- replaces beginFadeIn with g_IrisFadeType=0;
- on a dead hero waits only for Enter: no 4-second beginFadeOut or fadeIn wait;
- uses a flashlight max_distance of 32.0;
- resets special_view_active;
- clears field notes and releases puzzle graphics at start and end;
- closes the field notes and puzzle on a non-alive hero;
- forces the director when the camera index < 0;
- has Escape close the field notes and puzzle before the pause menu;
- calls resetIrisFade before skipCinematic.
There is no NewSet event, cursor bitmap, 640x480 switch or 3-frame clear.

BW2:
- drops jump and adds quick_turn and drop_item (key_drop) edges;
- reaches inventory through the hero's 'inventories' pointer;
- refuses next/prev weapon and weapon 1-3 when the hero casts to CDoc and a CDoc float field is > 0;
- maps weapons 1-3 to classes 0, 3 and 6;
- has no weapon 4/5 keys and no infrared key;
- keeps next-ammo and item-description.

BW2:
- uses the title_bw image drawn at 10,7 and XBLAIRMENU.WAV;
- centres lines across the full 0..0x280;
- sets each line's render alpha to 1 - |y-240|/240;
- restarts the scroll at 500 once it passes -2500, instead of ending.
Wrong: a missing credits.txt does not continue; it frees the image and returns, as nocedit does.

BW3:
- loads stats but never displays it, and plays no music (no resetSoundDevice or startSfx);
- splits lines with '\1' and '\2' into two columns at x 100 and 300, and centres other lines in 100..400;
- draws full-width black bars (0..0x27f) top and bottom;
- restarts the scroll at 480 once no line is visible;
- ends only on Escape.

BW1 defaults:
- model ecre.kfm (nocedit cre.kfm);
- weapon_type 10 (nocedit 2);
- fire_cooldown 0 (nocedit 1);
- can_attach_light 1 (nocedit 0);
- a new int at +0x58c set to 1;
- charge_level 2.0 (nocedit 30.0).
Same class version 1, so the data does not select them.
